  ($pp$Fort Funston$pp$, $pp$fort-funston$pp$, $pp$beach$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Golden Gate National Recreation Area$pp$, 37.716, -122.502, $pp$san_francisco$pp$::public.region, $pp$San Francisco$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$The Superintendent's Compendium lists Fort Funston for dogs leashed or under voice control, except the 12-acre closure in the northwest corner. Closed to dogs: the Habitat Protection Area, signed administrative areas, and the Coastal Trail at the Horse Trail / Great Highway intersection.$pp$, $pp$Voice control areas are defined by posted signs and park maps.$pp$, $pp$https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/management/superintendents-compendium.htm$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-07$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, array[$pp$cliffs$pp$, $pp$seasonal_closures$pp$]::text[], $pp$yes$pp$, $pp$none$pp$, null, 75, $pp$2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Crissy Field$pp$, $pp$crissy-field$pp$, $pp$beach$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Golden Gate National Recreation Area$pp$, 37.804, -122.463, $pp$san_francisco$pp$::public.region, $pp$San Francisco$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$The Superintendent's Compendium lists Crissy Field for dogs leashed or under voice control, excluding picnic areas. Dogs must be on leash in the Wildlife Protection Area July 1 to May 15 (36 CFR 7.97(d)). Closed to dogs: the Tidal Marsh and Lagoon.$pp$, $pp$Voice control areas are defined by posted signs and park maps.$pp$, $pp$https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/management/superintendents-compendium.htm$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-07$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, array[$pp$seasonal_closures$pp$]::text[], $pp$yes$pp$, $pp$none$pp$, null, 60, $pp$2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
