  ($pp$Big Break Regional Shoreline$pp$, $pp$big-break-regional-shoreline$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$East Bay Regional Park District$pp$, 38.0057, -121.7322, $pp$east_bay_north$pp$::public.region, $pp$Oakley$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$District-wide rule: dogs may be off leash in open space and undeveloped areas if they are in view and under voice control, and must return to leash when called. Leash (6 ft max) is required in developed areas, parking lots, picnic areas, grazing areas and for the first 200 ft of a trailhead. Dogs are not allowed at any swimming pool, beach, wetland, marsh or designated nature study area.$pp$, $pp$This rule comes from the district-wide dogs page; the park's own page lists dogs among its activities. Posted signs override.$pp$, $pp$https://ebparks.org/dogs$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
