  ($pp$Vasona Lake County Park$pp$, $pp$vasona-lake-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.2362, -121.9287, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$Los Gatos$pp$, $pp$leash_required$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$Dogs are welcome on a leash, and owners are expected to pick up droppings. Santa Clara County Parks says dogs are not allowed in some areas (playgrounds, historic sites, visitor centers, archery ranges and some trails); those areas are posted "No Dogs". Where there is no sign, keep your dog on a leash.$pp$, null, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/vasona-lake-county-park$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Villa Montalvo$pp$, $pp$villa-montalvo$pp$, $pp$trail$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.2437, -122.031, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$Saratoga$pp$, $pp$leash_required$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$Dogs on a 6-foot leash are allowed on the upper trails, which the county manages. Dogs are restricted from the botanical gardens and grounds of Villa Montalvo. Santa Clara County Parks says dogs are not allowed in some areas (playgrounds, historic sites, visitor centers, archery ranges and some trails); those areas are posted "No Dogs". Where there is no sign, keep your dog on a leash.$pp$, null, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/villa-montalvo$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Ed R. Levin County Park$pp$, $pp$ed-r-levin-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.4474, -121.8445, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$Milpitas$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$The park has a large fenced off-leash dog park for large and small dogs, owned and operated by the City of Milpitas. Elsewhere, dogs are allowed on leash in parking lots, picnic areas and on all trails north of Calaveras Road. Santa Clara County Parks says dogs are not allowed in some areas (playgrounds, historic sites, visitor centers, archery ranges and some trails); those areas are posted "No Dogs". Where there is no sign, keep your dog on a leash.$pp$, $pp$Off-leash only inside the fenced dog park. Leash required everywhere else.$pp$, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/ed-r-levin-county-park$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Hellyer County Park$pp$, $pp$hellyer-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.2843, -121.8146, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$San Jose$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$The park has a fenced off-leash dog area on the north side of the park, off Highway 101 at the Hellyer Avenue exit; elsewhere dogs must be on a 6-foot leash. Santa Clara County Parks says dogs are not allowed in some areas (playgrounds, historic sites, visitor centers, archery ranges and some trails); those areas are posted "No Dogs". Where there is no sign, keep your dog on a leash.$pp$, $pp$Off-leash only inside the fenced dog area. Off-leash areas close one day each week for maintenance.$pp$, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/hellyer-county-park$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Los Gatos Creek County Park$pp$, $pp$los-gatos-creek-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.2682, -121.9531, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$Campbell$pp$, $pp$off_leash_zones$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$The park has two fenced off-leash dog areas (small and large dogs) off Dell Avenue; elsewhere dogs must be on a 6-foot leash. Santa Clara County Parks says dogs are not allowed in some areas (playgrounds, historic sites, visitor centers, archery ranges and some trails); those areas are posted "No Dogs". Where there is no sign, keep your dog on a leash.$pp$, $pp$Off-leash only inside the fenced dog areas. Off-leash areas close one day each week for maintenance.$pp$, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/los-gatos-creek-county-park$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Alviso Marina County Park$pp$, $pp$alviso-marina-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.43, -121.9795, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$San Jose$pp$, $pp$no_dogs$pp$::public.dog_status, $pp$Dogs, drones and walking near the pond's edge are strictly prohibited. Stay on designated trails and away from the salt ponds to protect migratory birds and other wildlife.$pp$, null, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/alviso-marina-county-park$pp$, $pp$verified$pp$::public.verification_status, $pp$2026-11-16$pp$::date, $pp$claude (official page fetch), pending human review$pp$, null, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
  ($pp$Anderson Lake County Park$pp$, $pp$anderson-lake-county-park$pp$, $pp$park$pp$::public.place_type, $pp$Santa Clara County Parks$pp$, 37.1652, -121.6461, $pp$south_bay$pp$::public.region, $pp$Morgan Hill$pp$, null, null, null, $pp$https://parks.santaclaracounty.gov/locations/anderson-lake-county-park$pp$, $pp$needs_verification$pp$::public.verification_status, null, null, $pp$The county's page for this park does not say whether dogs are allowed. County parks generally allow dogs on a 6-foot leash, but this one does not list it.$pp$, 90, $pp$editorial$pp$, '{}'::text[], null, null, null, null, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz, $pp$2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z$pp$::timestamptz),
